MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 2032721509}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 3ff6acaa8b9f1994499dd387e6188532, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  Comments: "This scene demonstrates how Timeflow can be integrated with Unity Timeline
    so that both are synchronized with one another. In this example, the BlueCube
    is animated using Timeflow while the RedSphere is animated using Timeline. \n\nPlease
    note that this integration is only needed if you require Timeline and Timeflow
    to play in unison. Otherwise, both Timeflow and Timeline can be used in the same
    scene and will play separately (or in parallel). Since Timeflow is based on an
    entirely different timing system there is no conflict with sequences controlled
    by Timeline.\n\nThis integration requries adding Timeflow as a playback track
    in Timeline and configuring the Timeflow settings to synchronize with the director.
    Once the configuration has been set, either the Timeflow or Timeline window may
    be used to playback and preview animations and both will play with the same unified
    time.\n\nPlease refer to the documentation linked below for further information.\n\nTimeline
    Integration Documentation:\nhttps://axongenesis.gitbook.io/timeflow/reference/examples/timeline-integration"
  Warning: 
  URLTitle: 
  URL: 
  URL2Title: 
  URL2: 
